-- Creating a navigation profile (ako/mxcli-maintenance §7).
--
-- Mendix routes a phone to a Phone PROFILE on the User-Agent, not on viewport
-- width, so device-specific pages need the profile to exist. Before this,
-- CREATE OR REPLACE NAVIGATION could only ever REPLACE a stored profile:
--
--   Error: navigation profile not found: Phone (available: Responsive)
--
-- and nothing else in mxcli added one, which put a whole class of app out of
-- reach. A profile is now created when the name is one of Mendix's fixed web
-- kinds; an invented name is still an error, because a profile the platform
-- does not define can never route.
--
-- The shape is pinned against Studio Pro 11.14 over PED, measured by adding a
-- profile through Studio Pro's OWN model API and reading back what it filled
-- in. That is the part worth stating: the reference project's Phone profile
-- carries {Precaching: true, InstallPrompt: true}, but a profile Studio Pro has
-- just created stores ProgressiveWebAppSettings as null. Copying the former
-- would have turned precaching on for every profile mxcli creates.

create or replace navigation Phone
  home page MyFirstModule.Home_Web
  menu (
    menu item 'Home' page MyFirstModule.Home_Web;
  );

create or replace navigation Tablet
  home page MyFirstModule.Home_Web
  menu (
    menu item 'Home' page MyFirstModule.Home_Web;
  );

-- Re-running is an update, not a duplicate: the second run reports 'updated'.
create or replace navigation Phone
  home page MyFirstModule.Home_Web
  menu (
    menu item 'Home' page MyFirstModule.Home_Web;
  );

-- Each device kind has an offline twin. An offline profile is not a different
-- document -- measured over PED, a freshly created PhoneOffline stores exactly
-- the same keys as a Phone and differs only in Kind and Name.
--
-- What changes is what Mendix then demands of the pages the profile can reach:
-- an attribute may be bound across at most ONE association hop, and a longer
-- path is CE6206. Creating the profile reports the documents in the project
-- that already exceed that, because those pages were valid until this statement
-- ran and the build failure would otherwise turn up with no visible connection
-- to it.
create or replace navigation TabletOffline
  home page MyFirstModule.Home_Web
  menu (
    menu item 'Home' page MyFirstModule.Home_Web;
  );

create or replace navigation PhoneOffline
  home page MyFirstModule.Home_Web
  menu (
    menu item 'Home' page MyFirstModule.Home_Web;
  );

show navigation;
